      "options": {
        "content": "## What to Watch\n- CPU or Memory > 85% sustained\n- Disk usage > 85% (/, AnishSSD, Time Machine)\n- Ping loss > 2% or latency spikes\n- Wi\u2011Fi RSSI below -70 dBm or SNR below 20 dB\n",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "What to Watch",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "description": "High\u2011level summary panel for quick health checks. Use this to see if anything needs attention at a glance.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "content": "",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "KPI Strip",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows how busy your computer\u2019s brain (CPU) is. Higher values mean more work. If it stays high (>85%) for several minutes, apps may lag. Good for spotting heavy background tasks.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "max": 100,
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 70
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 85
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "area",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "((1 - avg(rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode=\"idle\"}[5m])) by (instance)) * 100) or on() vector(0)"
        }
      ],
      "title": "CPU %",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows how much RAM is in use. Higher values mean less free memory for new apps. Sustained high memory usage can cause slowdowns and app switching delays.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "max": 100,
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 70
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 85
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 4,
        "y": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "area",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "((node_memory_total_bytes - node_memory_free_bytes - node_memory_inactive_bytes - node_memory_purgeable_bytes) / node_memory_total_bytes * 100) or on() vector(0)"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Memory %",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "description": "Single, easy\u2011to\u2011read value. Useful for quick checks and thresholds.",
      "fieldConfig": {
